## A Common Philosophy

Although these frameworks address different clinical conditions, they share a common philosophy:

- Understand the underlying disease rather than treating symptoms alone.
- Establish an objective clinical baseline.
- Identify individual risk factors.
- Use appropriate diagnostic investigations.
- Develop personalised, evidence-based treatment strategies.
- Monitor outcomes and modify treatment when necessary.

The objective is to make complex clinical decisions more structured, transparent and patient-centred.

